# Working docs — kept local, not published.
#
# The published set is deliberately minimal: README, LICENSE, CHANGELOG,
# CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, and third-party notices. Everything below is written
# for us, and publishing it would either help nobody or actively help the wrong
# person:
#
#   HISTORY.md  dev log; names signing-key paths, how CI secrets are arranged,
#               and specifics of the maintainer's machine. Individually
#               harmless, collectively a map.
#   LAUNCH.md   release checklist; an itemised list of the project's soft spots.
#   PLAN.md     internal current-state and architecture notes.
#   TESTING.md  test-bench rationale; CONTRIBUTING carries the part a
#               contributor actually needs.
#   BRIEF-*     licensing / market / revenue briefs. States monetization
#               intent and license-change options, and inventories the
#               project's commercial soft spots. Publishing it would hand a
#               competitor the strategy and read to users as a rug pull
#               announced in advance.
#
# Note these were public before 2026-08-04, so they remain in git history.
# Removing them from HEAD stops new detail accruing; it doesn't erase the old.
# The signing key itself was never committed (*.key, above), which is the
# protection that actually matters.
HISTORY.md
LAUNCH.md
PLAN.md
TESTING.md
BRIEF-*.html
